# Skill bundles MUST ship their scripts, assets and data.
#
# Process Studio only executes scripts that live inside the skill bundle. A
# skill published without them fails at run time with:
#     Script invocation blocked: Skill file is outside the skill bundle
#
# This file previously excluded `*.py`, `skills/*/scripts/`, `skills/*/src/`,
# `skills/*/requirements.txt`, `skills/*/tests/`, `skills/*/evals/`,
# `skills/*/examples/`, `skills/*/core/` and `skills/*/templates/` -- the note
# said it was to stop Process Studio flagging package-name strings in .py
# files. The cost was that every affected skill shipped as documentation only
# and could not run at all. A scanner warning is cheaper than a dead skill, so
# those rules are gone.
#
# Keep out only genuine build output and OS clutter.

# Python build artefacts (regenerated on first run)
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/

# JS dependencies (restored with npm install)
node_modules/
skills/*/node_modules/

# Archives and large binaries do not belong in a skills repo
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.7z

# OS and Drive clutter
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*~
*.tmp
*.bak
*.swp

# Editor state
.vscode/
.idea/
